# groupon-mcp reads Groupon's public consumer endpoint with no API key or auth.
# No environment variables are required for the read-path (search / browse /
# deal detail / categories) — those boot and run with no credentials.

# ── Cart / purchase path (STDIO server only) ────────────────────────────────
# Cart operations (view cart, add to cart, clear cart) hit the SAME endpoint as
# the reads but require your AUTHENTICATED Groupon SESSION COOKIE. Verified: the
# cookie ALONE authorizes cart ops (no CSRF header / no fraud token).
#
# You normally do NOT set this: with the fetchproxy/Transporter browser bridge,
# the cart client lifts the session `Cookie` header from your signed-in
# groupon.com tab automatically on the first cart call. Set it only for local
# dev without the bridge — paste the full `Cookie:` request header from a
# signed-in www.groupon.com /mobilenextapi/graphql request (DevTools → Network).
# This is a secret — .env is gitignored; never commit it.
# GROUPON_SESSION_COOKIE=

# Set to 1/true to DISABLE the fetchproxy browser-bridge fallback (then the cart
# path relies solely on GROUPON_SESSION_COOKIE above).
# GROUPON_DISABLE_FETCHPROXY=

# Override the GraphQL endpoint (defaults to https://www.groupon.com/mobilenextapi/graphql).
# GROUPON_GRAPHQL_URL=

# Response-cache TTL for reads in seconds (0 = off; default 60).
# GROUPON_CACHE_TTL=
